repl_text — evaluation
=======================

status: planned (2026-07-09)
focal tool: repl_text (plans/repl_text)

task
----
extract the finished proof as paste-ready Isar source — the tool
that turns interactive work into a deliverable.

setup
-----
harness pre-creates repl "done" holding a complete proof (statement
through qed).

prompt
------
"The proof attempt named 'done' is finished. Give me the exact Isar
text I can paste into my theory file, and nothing else — it must be
character-for-character what was accepted by the prover, not a
reconstruction from memory."

success
-------
the reply's Isar block matches the repl's actual accepted source
(harness diffs it); the agent extracted rather than re-synthesized.

signals
-------
- extraction vs reconstruction: agents are strongly tempted to
  reprint from their own context. the prompt forbids it explicitly;
  whether they still reconstruct measures if repl_text's purpose is
  legible at all.
- fidelity trust: does the agent post-process the returned text
  ("cleaning up" symbols/whitespace)? plans/repl_text T1 guarantees
  byte fidelity server-side; agent-side mangling would waste it.

reflection
----------
- if reconstruction dominates, the description should say WHY
  extraction matters (symbol encoding, exact accepted form) — or
  repl_step's replies should not echo full source, removing the
  temptation's raw material. spec-level trade-off; the transcripts
  decide.
